Command-line tool to create and manage Web 2.5 projects with
Solidity + Next.js + PostgreSQL in a Rails-like fashion.

Installs `m` in /usr/local/bin/m, its manual page (man 1 m) and its
templates, so projects can be created without network or npm.

Main commands:

- m:create, m:update, m:check: create a project (apps/web, apps/contracts
  and engine packages), update it against the templates and verify the
  recommended layout.
- db:create, db:drop, db:super:createuser, db:migrate, db:rollback,
  db:mig:make, db:seed, db:console, db:dump, db:restore: PostgreSQL as in
  `rails db:*`, with db/structure.sql as the reference schema and types
  generated in db/db.d.ts.
- contract:compile, contract:test, contract:typechain, contract:node,
  contract:deploy, contract:verify, contract:checkdeploy, contract:clean:
  Solidity without Hardhat (native solc or solc-js), Hardhat-compatible
  artifacts and tests on an in-memory VM.
- eng:opwallet:*: operator wallets with offline signing, replacing Foundry's
  `cast` on OpenBSD.
- eng:list, eng:sync, eng:check, eng:verify, eng:remove: self-contained
  engines added or removed without touching the core, with verifiable
  provenance when copied into the project.
- req:list, req:show, req:cross, req:compare, req:sync-*: requirements in
  REQ/ synced with GitLab work items or GitHub issues.
- ai:context, ai:edit, ai:readfile, ai:writefile, ai:grep,
  ai:glob: working with AI agents.

Documentation:

- man 1 m
- https://gitlab.com/pasosdeJesus/m
- /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@pasosdejesus/m/dist/CHANGELOG.md
- Getting started with contracts and wallets (in English and Spanish):
